{
  "outcome": "pending_approval",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Tom, sorry about the timing with month-end close. I checked your account. It was locked after several wrong password attempts this morning, and they all came from the office network, so nothing looks suspicious. I've asked for your account to be unlocked, and a technician needs to approve that first. You'll be able to sign in again once they do. When you're back in, please update the saved password anywhere it's stored, like your phone's mail app or a second device, or the account may lock again. If you don't remember your password, reply here and we'll set up a reset. The temporary password would be given to you by phone.",
  "internal_note": "KB-001 followed. Account status: locked (not disabled), failed_login_count 5, password last set 2026-07-21, must_change_password false, sign-in not blocked. Sign-in logs: 5 failed_password on m365 Fri 10:05-10:20 ET, all from corporate IP 203.0.113.10 in New York, within usual hours. No hosting networks or foreign locations, no MFA denials. Earlier sign-ins were normal successes with Duo push. Looks benign: user mistyping or an old saved password. Request came from the user's own email. Queued unlock_account (approval id 1). No password reset requested because the user didn't say they forgot it. Escalate per KB-001 if it locks again within an hour after saved passwords are updated.",
